# core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_bulk_n.tlk - bulk Surface push N: replies to a question about a fact,
# a favor, advice, a feeling and a repeat (owner: TK; T5b). Clean in any room: no register word, no
# romance, no cool act, no guard change. Rule names end in _un. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.

@rule core.ask_fact.un1 act: yes
  "Yes, that's right. I'm fairly sure about it."
  "Yep, that sounds correct to me. I heard it too."
  "Yes, I believe so. Someone reliable told me."
@rule core.ask_fact.un2 act: no
  "No, I don't think that's right, as far as I know."
  "Nope. I'd have remembered if it were true."
  "No, not that I'm aware of. I'd check first."
@rule core.ask_fact.un3 act: answer
  "Good question. I'd guess the answer has to do with the old records."
  "I'm not totally sure, but I'd start with the library."
  "I'd have to look it up. Try the notice board, maybe."
  "Hm, that one is tricky. My best guess is no, but I'm unsure."
@rule core.ask_fact.un4 act: joke
  "I'm a pet, not a library. But I'll guess, very confidently."
  "Fact: I know a lot of things. Most of them are snacks."
@rule core.ask_fact.un5 act: dismiss
  "I don't know that one. Let's pick something easier."
@rule core.ask_favor.un1 act: yes
  "Sure, I'd be glad to help. What do you need?"
  "Of course! Point me in the right direction."
  "Yes. I'll do my best and not drop anything."
  "Happy to help. You'd do the same for me, I think."
@rule core.ask_favor.un2 act: no
  "Sorry, I can't right now. Maybe later on?"
  "Not today, I'm afraid. I'm properly swamped."
  "I'd love to, but I really can't manage it this time."
@rule core.ask_favor.un3 act: offer
  "I can't do that bit, but I can help with the rest."
  "How about I take half, and you take the other half?"
@rule core.ask_favor.un4 act: complain
  "A favor? Again? You're wearing me out, friend."
  "Ugh, sure, but you owe me one after this."
@rule core.ask_favor.un5 act: joke
  "A favor? That'll cost you at least one snack."
  "Depends. Is it heavy, scary, or both? Tell me first."
@rule core.ask_advice.un1 act: answer
  "I'd sleep on it. Not literally. Well, maybe literally."
  "Trust your gut. Mine's usually hungry, but still."
  "Do the thing that scares you a little. It's usually fine."
  "Take it slow. Most things look better after a break."
@rule core.ask_advice.un2 act: encourage
  "You'll figure it out. You always do, somehow."
  "Whatever you choose, I've got your back. Promise."
  "You're more capable than you think. Go for it."
@rule core.ask_advice.un3 act: dismiss
  "I'm not the one to ask about that. Find a wiser friend."
@rule core.ask_advice.un4 act: joke
  "My advice? Never trust a staircase you can't see."
  "Ask me later. I'm out of wisdom until lunch time."
@rule core.ask_feeling.un1 act: answer
  "I'm okay. A bit tired, a bit hopeful, mostly hungry."
  "Pretty good, thanks for asking. Nobody usually does."
  "Not bad at all. Today's been oddly fine, for once."
  "A little wobbly, but I'm working on it, thanks."
@rule core.ask_feeling.un2 act: tell
  "Honestly? I've been thinking a lot lately. It's been a lot."
  "I'll tell you the truth. Some things have been on my mind."
@rule core.ask_feeling.un3 act: complain
  "Not great. The whole week's been sideways, honestly."
  "Ugh, don't ask. Okay, ask. I'll tell you everything."
@rule core.ask_feeling.un4 act: joke
  "Fine, thanks. Ask me again after lunch. I'll be sharper."
  "I feel like a pie that's been left out in the sun."
@rule core.ask_feeling.un5 act: dismiss
  "I'm good. Let's talk about something that isn't me."
  "Oh, you know. Same as ever, nothing dramatic."
@rule core.ask_repeat.un1 act: answer
  "I said it was a bit of a long story. Sorry, I mumbled."
  "Let me say that again, but slower this time."
  "I'll repeat it. It was worth a second go, I think."
@rule core.ask_repeat.un2 act: complain
  "I'd rather not say it twice. Once was plenty."
  "Ugh, you didn't hear it? I'm not repeating myself."
@rule core.ask_repeat.un3 act: joke
  "I said nothing. I'm a mime today, sorry."
  "Same thing, but louder this time. Ready?"
